  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The amount of charge in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>&nbsp;(Faraday) required to obtain one mole of iron from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is ______. (Round off the answer to the nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a mixed oxide(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mover><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>)</p><p>The net change in oxidation can be calculated as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow></mover><mn>3</mn><mi>Fe</mi></math></p><p>For 3 moles of formation of iron, 8 moles of electrons are involved.</p><p>One mole of electrons charge is called one Faraday.</p><p>Charge for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
